pixelbin · grund.toml · v2

kinds and places
  ART    kind                         .specify/memory/constitution.md
  RULE   kind                         .specify/memory/rules.md
  SPEC   kind                         specs/001-photo-upload/spec.md, specs/002-album-share/spec.md
           field clarifications       `## clarifications: Clarifications` (may, first)
           field user-scenarios       `## user-scenarios: User Scenarios & Testing *(mandatory)*` (must, directly after clarifications)
           field requirements         `## requirements: Requirements *(mandatory)*` (must, directly after user-scenarios)
           field success-criteria     `## success-criteria: Success Criteria *(mandatory)*` (must, directly after requirements)
           field assumptions          `## assumptions: Assumptions` (may, directly after success-criteria)
           closed                     no other chapter except numbered ones (must)
  PLAN   kind                         specs/001-photo-upload/plan.md, specs/002-album-share/plan.md
           field summary              `## summary: Summary` (must, first)
           field technical-context    `## technical-context: Technical Context` (must, directly after summary)
           field constitution-check   `## constitution-check: Constitution Check` (must, directly after technical-context)
           field project-structure    `## project-structure: Project Structure` (must, directly after constitution-check)
           field complexity-tracking  `## complexity-tracking: Complexity Tracking` (may, directly after project-structure)
           closed                     no other chapter except numbered ones (must)
  tasks  place                        specs/001-photo-upload/tasks.md, specs/002-album-share/tasks.md
  test   place                        tests/
  code   complement                   src/

citations                             grounded
  ART    may       ART (itself)
         may       RULE
         must not  everything else
  RULE   —
  SPEC   may       SPEC (itself)
         may       ART
         must not  everything else
  PLAN   must      SPEC
  tasks  must      SPEC|PLAN          must · h3
  test   must      SPEC               must · file
  code   must      SPEC               must · file

must = check error · warn = check warning · should = suggestion (check --suggestions)
may = allowed · must not / warn not / should not = forbidden at that strength
A|B = one obligation, met by citing either · — = no direction rule names it
## = under a declaration written # <ID>: … · a field always sits one level below its declaration's heading
